{"id": "EUVD-2026-101574", "enisaUuid": "40b07cc9-ca08-3d40-98eb-86f31fb0cf4d", "description": "Blinko through 1.8.8 contains a broken access control vulnerability in the /api/file route that allows authenticated users to read other users' private attachments due to a flawed owner check. Attackers can supply another user's stored filename, following a basename plus millisecond-timestamp pattern, to download private, non-shared attachments.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T18:48:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T14:26:13", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/blinko-attachment-accountid-idor", "https://github.com/blinkospace/blinko/blob/178e4b3538a21823a50ac2481e653d56cb1ffa86/server/routerExpress/file/file.ts#L148", "https://github.com/blinkospace/blinko", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/blinko-through-1.8.8-private-attachment-read-via-api-file-route"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110774", "GHSA-62f6-6f4g-pr5m"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "34e24aca-df23-38fd-8e5f-c8d413531e1c", "product": {"name": "blinko", "vendor": {"name": "blinkospace"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.8.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "479672f7-c851-3874-b27d-09f7c5a79b67", "vendor": {"name": "blinkospace"}}], "isExploited": false}